# AI:ML Biased

This app explains how data can be biased and how machine learning models trained on such biased data can lead to biased outcomes.

## What is Data Bias?

Data bias refers to the presence of unfair or prejudiced information in the training dataset. This can happen due to underrepresentation of certain groups, historical prejudices, or sampling errors.

## Impact on Training

When a model is trained on biased data, it learns and perpetuates these biases. For instance, a hiring algorithm trained on data from a biased hiring process might favor certain demographics, leading to discriminatory results.


## Purpose of This App

This application aims to illustrate these concepts through examples and simulations, promoting awareness and best practices for fair AI development.